§§ `s 3: ordinary pay`

`NONE` MEANS `not provided`
`FIXED` MEANS `provided, with a cash value fixed by the terms of my employment`
`UNFIXED` MEANS `provided, with no cash value fixed`

-- Time rate: the greater of 1500 now and 1400 over 5 years, with the 12-month bonuses (100): 1600.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `NONE` 0 `NONE` 0 200000 EQUALS 1600
-- The 5-year figure greater: 1500 with the 5-year bonuses (80): 1580.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1400 1500 0 0 100 80 `NONE` 0 `NONE` 0 200000 EQUALS 1580
-- A tie takes the first (fork F8): 1500 + 100.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1500 0 0 100 80 `NONE` 0 `NONE` 0 200000 EQUALS 1600
-- Not a time rate: the greater of 1200 and 1300, with the 5-year bonuses (70): 1370.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` FALSE 0 0 1200 1300 50 70 `NONE` 0 `NONE` 0 200000 EQUALS 1370
-- Board and lodging with no value fixed: $15 + $5 (s 3(2)(d)): 1620.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `UNFIXED` 0 `UNFIXED` 0 200000 EQUALS 1620
-- Board fixed at $40, no lodging: 1640.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `FIXED` 40 `NONE` 0 200000 EQUALS 1640
-- s 3(2C): 1500 x 52 = 78000 exceeds 77999, so bonuses are out: 1500; at exactly 78000 they stay: 1600.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `NONE` 0 `NONE` 0 77999 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `NONE` 0 `NONE` 0 78000 EQUALS 1600
-- With board and lodging (1520 x 52 = 79040): at 79040 bonuses stay (1620); at 79039 they go (1520).
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `UNFIXED` 0 `UNFIXED` 0 79040 EQUALS 1620
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` TRUE 1500 1400 0 0 100 80 `UNFIXED` 0 `UNFIXED` 0 79039 EQUALS 1520

§§ `s 4(3), (3AA), (3A): taking the leave`

`ONE` MEANS `in one continuous period`
`SPLIT` MEANS `in two or more separate periods`
`ADVANCE` MEANS `in advance, before I am entitled to it`
`LATER` MEANS `from a later date agreed with my employer`

#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `ONE` FALSE 60 EQUALS `yes: the leave is given and taken in one continuous period, as soon as practicable having regard to the needs of the employer's establishment (s 4(3)(a), (b))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `SPLIT` TRUE 1 EQUALS `yes: with your employer's agreement you may take it in two or more separate periods, each of at least 1 day (s 4(3)(b), (3AA))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `SPLIT` TRUE (1 DIVIDED BY 2) EQUALS `no: each period must be at least 1 day (s 4(3AA), (3A)); for a worker with no fixed weekly hours a day is worked out under s 4(3B)`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `SPLIT` FALSE 5 EQUALS `no: separate periods need your employer's agreement; otherwise the leave is taken in one continuous period (s 4(3)(b), (3AA))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `ADVANCE` TRUE 5 EQUALS `yes: with your employer's agreement you may take a period of at least 1 day in advance; on termination your employer may deduct pay for leave taken beyond your entitlement (s 4(3A), (5)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `ADVANCE` TRUE (1 DIVIDED BY 2) EQUALS `no: each period must be at least 1 day (s 4(3AA), (3A)); for a worker with no fixed weekly hours a day is worked out under s 4(3B)`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `ADVANCE` FALSE 5 EQUALS `no: leave in advance needs your employer's agreement (s 4(3A))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `LATER` TRUE 60 EQUALS `yes: you and your employer have agreed to postpone the leave, so it is taken from the agreed date (s 4(3)(a)); you may also agree that your ordinary pay is fixed as at the date of that agreement (s 3(2B))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave this way` `LATER` FALSE 60 EQUALS `no: postponing the leave needs an agreement with your employer; otherwise it is given and taken as soon as practicable (s 4(3)(a))`

